Step 6: Final execution order
Keep this table ready for your practical exam.
Order	Filename	Operation
1	demo_create_mongo_db.js	Create database
2	demo_mongodb_createcollection.js	Create collection
3	demo_mongodb_insert_multiple.js	Insert documents
4	demo_mongodb_find.js	Access documents

Execute all commands in the VS Code terminal:
node demo_create_mongo_db.js
node demo_mongodb_createcollection.js
node demo_mongodb_insert_multiple.js
node demo_mongodb_find.js


Important practical exam notes
- Start MongoDB Server before running the programs.
- Install mongodb@4.17.2 to support the callback syntax used in your syllabus.
- Run the programs in the correct order.
- Do not repeatedly execute the insertion program, otherwise duplicate records will be inserted.
- Remember to use db.close() after completing each operation.

One-line memory trick:

Connect → Create Database → Create Collection → Insert Documents → Find Documents.
